; Two names with the same data and very different TTLs.  How long the
; cache is allowed to keep each of them is the only thing that tells
; them apart, so how often this server is asked for each one says what
; the cache did with the number it was given.
;
; a.t.e-ontap.com asks the same thing of an ISP's resolver: 「ISPのDNS
; キャッシュサーバはTTLを越えてキャッシュを保持するか?」
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@	IN	SOA	ns.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@	IN	NS	ns.example.
ns	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
long	3600	IN	A	192.0.2.1
brief	2	IN	A	192.0.2.2
